Most warlocks in Classic WoW use Voidwalkers for **solo survivability and tanking**, not because they are better for damage.

While the Succubus deals more damage, the Voidwalker's **Torment** (taunt) and **Sacrifice** (shield) allow the Warlock to safely solo elite mobs, pull multiple enemies, and survive mistakes that would kill a player with a Succubus. The Voidwalker effectively acts as a dedicated tank, whereas the Succubus relies on crowd control which can fail against non-humanoids or multiple targets. [end of text]


